text:
elayne: Heads-up from today's UX pass on the Console toolbar: the primary button is sitting almost flush with the compact search field at 320px. Feels cramped and the icon+label combo looks off. Screenshot: https://img.redwood.example/console/toolbar-cramped.png
mohit: yep that's the compact spacing token in use. Current token is `--space-compact: 6px`. For toolbar controls i think we should widen to ~10px to preserve touch rhythm.
frank: instead of changing `--space-compact` globally, can we add `--space-toolbar-inline: 10px` so other compact contexts don't regress?
claire: strongly +1 to namespace token. clearer intent and lower blast radius. Also a copy consistency note: buttons in the toolbar read "Launch" but the modal primary says "Start job". pick one.
elayne: i'd prefer "Launch job" for the toolbar and modal primary. Feels slightly more descriptive for background run actions.
mohit: agreed. I'll add `--space-toolbar-inline` to tokens and update Storybook with a 320px toolbar example. Quick CSS patch:```css
:root {
  --space-toolbar-inline: 10px;
}
.toolbar .cta + .cta {
  margin-left: var(--space-toolbar-inline);
}
```
frank: accessibility nit: when toolbar triggers the modal, focus isn't moving into the modal on iOS VoiceOver. Also, error toasts don't announce because we set role=region currently. For errors we should use `role=alert` or `aria-live=assertive`, and make error toasts keyboard-focusable so users can hit Retry.
claire: sample modal open handler suggestion:
```js
function onModalOpen(modal) {
  modal.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');
  modal.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
  const focusTarget = modal.querySelector('[data-autofocus]') || modal.querySelector('button, [href], input');
  if (focusTarget) focusTarget.focus();
}
```
mohit: and for toasts:```html
<div class="toast toast--error" role="alert" tabindex="0">Job failed to launch. <button aria-label="Retry launching job">Retry</button></div>
```
elayne: nice. also add an a11y story to Storybook that demonstrates focus landing in the modal and an error toast receiving focus. We'll add an automated axe run for those stories.
frank: small implementation test idea: snapshot the toolbar at 320px and run an accessibility smoke test in CI so if someone reverts the token we'll catch it.
claire: i'll update the copy tokens file to standardize on "Launch job" and push to Figma (file: Console - Interaction Tokens) once the token PR lands.
aria-bot: design token update queued: Console Tokens (file: https://figma.redwood.example/console-tokens)
mohit: plan: 1) add `--space-toolbar-inline: 10px` token + story at 320px, 2) patch Modal open focus trap + aria-modal, 3) make error toasts role=alert and tabindex=0 + story, 4) copy tokens -> "Launch job", 5) snapshot + axe smoke CI. i'll open one PR with the token + story and a follow-up PR for modal/toast fixes.
elayne: thanks folks, appreciate the quick sync. i'll review the PRs and run a manual NVDA pass after changes land.
